001
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000 | Speaker 1 | Female | Neutral
Gastric problems are very common, with at least one or two people in every family experiencing them at some point in their lifetime.

002
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000 | Speaker 1 | Female | Neutral
Doctor, how do you define this gastric problem according to Ayurveda?

003
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:20,000 | Speaker 2 | Female | Neutral
When we talk about gastric problems, we refer to them as a lifestyle disorder. Almost everyone nowadays suffers from it due to their lifestyle or food habits.

004
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:32,000 | Speaker 2 | Female | Neutral
In Ayurveda, we call this Amla Pitta. This means that if Pitta dosha increases in your body, it becomes acidic. So, from that, you get Amla Pitta, which means you get acidity, as we say.

005
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:42,000 | Speaker 2 | Female | Neutral
According to Ayurveda, if we want to explain this, it is related to Annvaha Strotas (channels of food transport). So, there are many strotas. Acidity is more likely to occur due to the vitiation of Annvaha Strotas.

006
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,000 | Speaker 1 | Female | Neutral
Hmm, absolutely.

007
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:46,000 | Speaker 1 | Female | Neutral
So, the doctor was explaining to us what gastric problem means.

008
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:58,000 | Speaker 1 | Female | Neutral
You too might have experienced gastric problems due to various reasons. Now, is the main reason for this gastric problem the mistakes we make? Or what causes us to experience gastric problems?

009
00:00:58,000 --> 00:00:59,000 | Speaker 1 | Female | Neutral
Please explain this.

010
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,000 | Speaker 2 | Female | Neutral
Gastric problems primarily arise from us. This is because of your diet and lifestyle.

011
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:15,000 | Speaker 2 | Female | Neutral
If we go by Ayurveda, we talk about Viruddha Ahara (incompatible foods). For instance, consuming milk with curd, or eating sweet items after sour items.

012
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:23,000 | Speaker 2 | Female | Neutral
So, we consume such incompatible foods. Also, if we consume contaminated food, meaning unhygienic food, or if we don't eat on time,

013
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:31,000 | Speaker 2 | Female | Neutral
And also during certain seasons. For example, during particular seasons like Varsha and Sharad Ritu, the Pitta dosha in our body increases.

014
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:43,000 | Speaker 2 | Female | Neutral
So, in such situations, if you consume food in the same manner, meaning a lot of spicy foods, too many fried items, or coffee and tea, then there is a possibility of increased gastric issues.

015
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:56,000 | Speaker 2 | Female | Neutral
Another thing we talk about is suppression of natural urges. This means you might feel the urge to pass stool or urine, but some work comes up, and you can't go. If you hold it for a long time, there's a higher chance of developing gastric problems.

016
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:03,000 | Speaker 2 | Female | Neutral
Also, stress can lead to hormonal changes in the body, which can also cause you to face gastric problems.

017
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:13,000 | Speaker 1 | Female | Neutral
Absolutely. So, the doctor was explaining to us that gastric problems can arise due to mistakes we make, incompatible foods, consuming spicy food, or frequently drinking coffee and tea.

